WEBVTT

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:02.900
Are you a SMART fella,

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.933
or a FART smella?

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:06.433
Let's find OUT!

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.200
Okay,

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.000
a number series!

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:10.633
Three,

00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:11.233
six,

00:00:11.233 --> 00:00:11.833
twelve,

00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:12.433
twenty-four,

00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:13.633
and then...

00:00:13.633 --> 00:00:15.433
what comes next?

00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:16.033
A.

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:16.667
Thirty-six,

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:17.267
B.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:17.867
Forty-eight,

00:00:17.867 --> 00:00:18.467
C.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:19.067
Thirty,

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.267
or D.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:20.867
Forty-two?

00:00:20.867 --> 00:00:22.067
Five seconds!

00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:29.067
TIME'S UP!

00:00:29.733 --> 00:00:31.600
The answer is...

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.233
B,

00:00:32.233 --> 00:00:32.833
forty-eight!

00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:34.700
Each number doubles:

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.333
three,

00:00:35.333 --> 00:00:35.967
six,

00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:36.567
twelve,

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:37.200
twenty-four,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.933
so twenty-four times two is forty-eight.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.700
Check this out,

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.333
a word analogy!

00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:47.500
Day is to week,

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.633
as month is to...

00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:50.167
what?

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:50.700
A.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.267
Hour,

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:51.800
B.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:52.333
Minute,

00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:52.867
C.

00:00:52.867 --> 00:00:53.400
Year,

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.500
or D.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.033
Calendar?

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:56.100
Five seconds!

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:03.100
TIME'S UP!

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:04.100
It's...

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:04.433
C,

00:01:04.433 --> 00:01:04.800
year!

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.500
Seven days make a week,

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.533
and twelve months make a year.

00:01:08.533 --> 00:01:10.600
A month is part of a

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.633
year the way a day is

00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:14.000
part of a week.

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:16.600
Check this out,

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.500
fill in the blank!

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.900
After the long dry summer,

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.767
the once green field looked completely

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:26.633
blank with no plants left at

00:01:26.633 --> 00:01:27.100
all.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:27.600
A.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.067
Crowded,

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:28.533
B.

00:01:28.533 --> 00:01:29.033
Barren,

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:29.500
C.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:29.967
Frozen,

00:01:29.967 --> 00:01:30.933
or D.

00:01:30.933 --> 00:01:31.400
Cheerful?

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.367
Five seconds!

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:39.367
TIME'S UP!

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:40.500
It's...

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:40.967
B,

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:41.433
barren!

00:01:41.433 --> 00:01:44.267
With no plants left after a

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:45.200
dry summer,

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.000
the field is bare and empty.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.833
Barren means nothing can grow there.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:52.400
So,

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.433
are you smart or fart?

00:01:54.433 --> 00:01:56.867
Count up your correct answers to

00:01:56.867 --> 00:01:58.067
find your rank!

00:01:59.233 --> 00:01:59.567
So,

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:00.967
how did you do?

00:02:00.967 --> 00:02:02.333
Comment your score below,

00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:03.700
and follow for more!
